<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutb al-Din Mawdud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1170</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutb al-Din Mawdud was the Zengid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> from 1149 to 1170, a son of Zengi and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>. He generally supported his brother's campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> and governed Mosul and the Jazira, where his court patronised learning and building.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qutb-al-din-mawdud.jpg" alt="Qutb al-Din Mawdud" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Numismatic Society · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qutb_al-Din_Mawdud_ibn_Zengi,_al-Mawsil,_556_H.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
